Expands Math.BigMul(ulong, ulong, out ulong) and Math.BigMul(long, long, out long) on riscv64 into the
two instructions the M extension has for the full 64x64 product: `mul` for the low half (an ordinary
GT_MUL stored through the out pointer) and `mulhu` / `mulh` for the high half, carried by a new
GT_INTRINSIC NI_PRIMITIVE_MultiplyHigh[Unsigned] node (target intrinsic: LSRA and codegen cases, VN as an
opaque commutative function so equal products CSE). The managed body has no RISC-V path and falls back to
four 32x32 multiplies and about 20 shifts and adds; UInt256 multiplication (EVM MUL, 118 `mul` and no
`mulhu` in the Nethermind guest's OpMul) is built on it. The two CoreLib overloads gain [Intrinsic] so the
JIT sees the call; on every other target the JIT recognizes the name and leaves the call (and its
AggressiveInlining body) exactly as before. The (ulong, uint, out) and 32x32 overloads are untouched.

RISC-V64: Math.BigMul 64x64 -> mul + mulhu / mulh.

